# 24-Hour Digital Clock

A Python + Tkinter desktop clock focused on always-visible time tools: digital and analogue displays, alarms, stopwatch, countdown timer, world clock, compact HUD mode, screensaver mode, and system tray support.

## Features

- Digital and analogue clock display modes.
- 12-hour and 24-hour time formats.
- Optional date display with selectable date formats.
- Timezone selection using IANA timezone names.
- World clock list with live offsets.
- Alarm management with repeat modes:
  - Once
  - Daily
  - Weekdays
  - Weekends
  - Custom weekdays
- Alarm popups with snooze support.
- Stopwatch with lap tracking, split display, clipboard export, and text export.
- Countdown timer with presets and completion notifications.
- Pomodoro mode with automatic phase cycling.
- Configurable timer/alarm sounds (`System Beep` or custom `.wav` on Windows).
- Compact HUD mode with corner pinning and monitor selection.
- Fullscreen screensaver with drift animation and optional color cycling.
- System tray minimize/open/quit workflow.
- Theme selection (`dark`, `light`, `system`).
- Always-on-top toggle.
- Persistent settings and runtime session data.

